   "title": "NATO Differences Named in JP 3-09.3",
   "html": "<div class=\"callout nato\"><div class=\"ct\">NATO · Line titles</div><div><blockquote class=\"quote\"><p>Note: Allied Tactical Publication 3.3.2.1, TTP for Close Air Support and Air Interdiction, directs that NATO FACs will pass line titles for each line in a CAS brief.</p><p>When working with NATO FACs/JTACs, aircrews should expect to hear line titles being passed prior to each item in the CAS brief. This is a measure to reduce confusion when some CAS participants are non-native English language speakers. Consideration should be given to passing line titles during times where language barriers, communications jamming, or other conditions exist that may lead to confusion.</p><cite>JP 3-09.3, p. V-26</cite></blockquote></div></div><div class=\"callout nato\"><div class=\"ct\">NATO · Line 8</div><div><blockquote class=\"quote\"><p>Note: NATO Allied Tactical Publication 3.3.2.1, TTP for Close Air Support and Air Interdiction, requires Line 8 to be a mandatory readback item. When working with NATO FACs/JTACs, aircrew should be prepared to read back Line 8 as part of the mandatory readback items.</p><cite>JP 3-09.3, p. V-30</cite></blockquote></div></div>",
